\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, ye thankful people, come,
\par Raise the song of harvest home:
\par All is safely gathered in,
\par Ere the winter storms begin;
\par God our Maker doth provide
\par For our wants to be supplied:
\par Come to God's own temple, come,
\par Raise the song of harvest home!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. All the world is God's own field,
\par Fruit unto His praise to yield;
\par Wheat and tears together sown,
\par Unto joy or sorrow grown;
\par First the blade, and then the ear,
\par Then the full corn shall appear:
\par Grant, O harvest Lord, that we
\par Wholesome grain and pure may be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For the Lord our God shall come,
\par And shall take His harvest home;
\par From His field shall in that day
\par All offences purge away;
\par Give His angels charge at last
\par In the fire the tares to cast;
\par But the fruitful ears to store,
\par In His garner evermore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Even so, Lord, quickly come;
\par Bring Thy final harvest home:
\par Gather Thou Thy people in,
\par Free from sorrow, free from sin;
\par There, for ever purified,
\par In Thy garner to abide:
\par Come, with all Thine angels, come,
\par Raise the glorious harvest-home!
\par                                     Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

